## Phase 5: Structure Maintenance

⚠️ CRITICAL: MAINTAIN DIRECTORY STRUCTURE INTEGRITY ⚠️

- Always run structure validation script before commits:
  ```bash
  # Add to pre-commit hook
  npm run validate-structure
  ```

- Follow these structure rules:
  1. ALWAYS place new files in appropriate subdirectories of `src/`
  2. NEVER create new directories at root level
  3. NEVER create files with similar names in different paths (e.g., `Navigation.tsx` and `navigation.tsx`)
  4. ALWAYS use consistent casing:
     - Component files: PascalCase (MyComponent.tsx)
     - Non-component files: camelCase (myUtils.ts)
     - Directories: camelCase (components, screens)
  5. NEVER create duplicate functionality in different locations
  6. ALWAYS add new features to matching existing directories
  7. WHEN UNSURE about file placement, run directory check:
     ```bash
     # Show allowed directories for file placement
     npx ts-node scripts/check-file-placement.js --file=MyNewComponent.tsx
     ```

## Phase 6: Implementation Patterns

### Firebase Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// src/services/database/firebaseService.ts
import { initializeApp } from 'firebase/app';
import { getFirestore, enablePersistence, collection, doc, setDoc, getDoc } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { FIREBASE_CONFIG } from '../../constants/config';

// Initialize Firebase
const app = initializeApp(FIREBASE_CONFIG);
const db = getFirestore(app);

// Enable offline persistence
enablePersistence(db, { synchronizeTabs: true }).catch((err) => {
  console.error('Firebase persistence error:', err.code);
});

// Typed collection references
export const customersCollection = collection(db, 'customers');
export const petsCollection = collection(db, 'pets');
export const appointmentsCollection = collection(db, 'appointments');

// CRUD operations with error handling and offline support
export const createDocument = async <T>(collectionName: string, docId: string, data: T): Promise<void> => {
  try {
    await setDoc(doc(db, collectionName, docId), data, { merge: true });
    console.log(`Document ${docId} successfully written to ${collectionName}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error writing document to ${collectionName}:`, error);
    // Queue for offline sync if needed
    throw error;
  }
};

// Always include detailed error handling
```

### Google Maps Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// src/services/location/mapsService.ts
import { GOOGLE_MAPS_CONFIG } from '../../constants/config';
import * as Location from 'expo-location';
import { Client, TravelMode } from '@googlemaps/google-maps-services-js';

// Initialize the Google Maps client
const client = new Client({});

// Request location permissions early
export const requestLocationPermissions = async (): Promise<boolean> => {
  try {
    const { status } = await Location.requestForegroundPermissionsAsync();
    return status === 'granted';
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error requesting location permissions:', error);
    return false;
  }
};

// Calculate route between coordinates
export const calculateRoute = async (
  origins: [number, number][],
  destinations: [number, number][],
): Promise<any> => {
  try {
    const response = await client.distancematrix({
      params: {
        origins: origins.map(coord => `${coord[0]},${coord[1]}`),
        destinations: destinations.map(coord => `${coord[0]},${coord[1]}`),
        mode: TravelMode.driving,
        key: GOOGLE_MAPS_CONFIG.apiKey,
      },
    });
    
    return response.data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error calculating route:', error);
    // Implement offline fallback
    throw error;
  }
};

// Route optimization algorithm
export const optimizeRoute = (appointments: any[]): any[] => {
  // Implementation of traveling salesman problem algorithm
  // Return optimized appointment order
  return appointments.sort((a, b) => new Date(a.startTime).getTime() - new Date(b.startTime).getTime());
};
```

### Stripe Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// src/services/payments/stripeService.ts
import { initStripe } from '@stripe/stripe-react-native';
import { STRIPE_CONFIG } from '../../constants/config';

// Initialize Stripe
export const initializeStripe = async (): Promise<void> => {
  try {
    await initStripe({
      publishableKey: STRIPE_CONFIG.publishableKey,
      merchantIdentifier: 'merchant.com.waypoint',
    });
    console.log('Stripe initialized successfully');
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to initialize Stripe:', error);
    throw error;
  }
};

// Process payment
export const processPayment = async (amount: number, currency: string, customerId: string): Promise<any> => {
  try {
    // Implementation
    return { success: true };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Payment processing error:', error);
    // Handle offline case
    throw error;
  }
};

// Generate receipt
export const generateReceipt = async (paymentId: string): Promise<string> => {
  try {
    // Implementation
    return 'receipt_url';
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Receipt generation error:', error);
    throw error;
  }
};
```

## Phase 7: Release Preparation
❗ STOP AND VERIFY:
□ All tests pass with ≥80% coverage
□ No ESLint errors or warnings
□ No TypeScript errors
□ No circular dependencies
□ All features work offline
□ Firebase integration is working properly
□ Google Maps integration is working properly
□ Stripe payment processing is working properly
□ Synchronization works when connectivity is restored

Only after ALL checks pass can you prepare for release:
```bash
# Run final check
npm run check-all

# Build Android app
eas build --platform android --profile production
```

## Code Quality Requirements
- ✓ Components MUST have comprehensive tests
- ✓ All database operations MUST handle offline mode
- ✓ All network requests MUST use retry and queue mechanisms
- ✓ All screens MUST implement proper loading and error states
- ✓ All forms MUST include validation with Formik+Yup
- ✓ All API keys MUST be stored in environment variables
- ✓ Firebase security rules MUST be properly configured
- ✓ Stripe integration MUST use test keys in development
- ⛔️ NEVER skip tests before merging or releasing
- ⛔️ NEVER hardcode API keys in source code
- ⛔️ NEVER store sensitive data unencrypted

## Feature Requirements

### Firebase Requirements
- ✓ Authentication MUST include email/password and Google Sign-In
- ✓ Firestore security rules MUST restrict access properly
- ✓ Data model MUST follow NoSQL best practices
- ✓ Cloud Functions MUST handle background processing
- ✓ File storage MUST include retry logic for uploads
- ✓ Offline persistence MUST be enabled
- ✓ Firestore transactions MUST be used for critical operations

### Google Maps Requirements
- ✓ Maps MUST be cached for offline use
- ✓ Routes MUST be pre-calculated when possible
- ✓ ETA calculations MUST handle offline scenarios
- ✓ Location tracking MUST be battery-efficient
- ✓ Maps MUST display pet location markers with custom icons
- ✓ Routes MUST be color-coded for status (completed, upcoming)
- ✓ Optimize button MUST rearrange appointments efficiently

### Stripe Requirements
- ✓ Payment processing MUST work offline (queue for later)
- ✓ Receipts MUST be generated and shareable
- ✓ Webhooks MUST handle payment status updates
- ✓ Error handling MUST be comprehensive
- ✓ Test mode MUST be used during development
- ✓ Production keys MUST be restricted to production builds

### Offline Functionality
- ✓ All data operations MUST work offline
- ✓ Changes MUST be queued for sync when back online
- ✓ Conflict resolution strategy MUST be implemented
- ✓ Critical operations MUST have offline fallbacks
- ✓ Offline maps MUST be available for navigation
- ✓ Cached data MUST have expiration policies

### Customer Management
- ✓ Customer profiles MUST include contact info, address, notes
- ✓ Pet profiles MUST include breed, size, temperament, special needs
- ✓ Photos MUST be optimized for mobile storage
- ✓ Notes MUST sync bidirectionally
- ✓ Customer history MUST be searchable
- ✓ Contact methods MUST be integrated with device (call, text, email)

### Appointment Management
- ✓ Calendar MUST support day/week/month views
- ✓ Appointments MUST include travel time between locations
- ✓ Scheduling MUST prevent overlapping appointments
- ✓ Notifications MUST work offline
- ✓ Recurring appointments MUST be supported
- ✓ Appointment details MUST include service notes, duration, price

### UI Requirements
- ✓ UI MUST match the provided mockup for the Dispatch screen
- ✓ Map and appointment list MUST be responsive to different screen sizes
- ✓ All interactive elements MUST have minimum touch target size of 44x44
- ✓ Color contrast MUST meet accessibility standards
- ✓ Loading states MUST be shown during data fetching
- ✓ Error states MUST provide recovery options

## Commit Message Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

Allowed types:
- feat: New feature
- fix: Bug fix
- docs: Documentation
- style: Formatting
- refactor: Code restructuring
- perf: Performance improvements
- test: Adding tests
- build: Build system changes
- ci: CI configuration
- chore: Maintenance tasks

Scopes:
- customer
- pet
- appointment
- route
- payment
- auth
- ui
- offline
- sync
- firebase
- maps
- stripe

## Performance Benchmarks
- App startup: < 2 seconds
- Screen transition: < 300ms
- Offline data access: < 100ms
- Map rendering: < 500ms
- Battery usage: < 5% per hour of active use
- Storage: < 100MB base installation

## Security Requirements
- ✓ All API keys MUST be secured
- ✓ Customer data MUST be encrypted
- ✓ Payment information MUST NOT be stored locally
- ✓ Authentication MUST timeout after inactivity
- ✓ Firebase security rules MUST limit access appropriately
- ✓ JWT tokens MUST be securely stored
- ✓ No sensitive information in logs